+{"cell_id": "sha256:f41e41e60de25f758a5ec550cd65c0330b706e26ce1705e8c209f5cbbc75db9d", "chat_messages": [{"content": "You are writing one Python solution for a programming task. Return only raw Python code or one fenced python block. Do not explain the answer.", "role": "system"}, {"content": "Seed cell: sha256:f41e41e60de25f758a5ec550cd65c0330b706e26ce1705e8c209f5cbbc75db9d\nStrategy: edge_case_guarded\nWrite a Python solution that handles boundary cases first, then the general case. Keep parsing explicit and return only runnable code.\n\nTitle: Bitmask\nYou are given an integer N and a string S consisting of 0, 1, and ?.\nLet T be the set of values that can be obtained by replacing each ? in S with 0 or 1 and interpreting the result as a binary integer.\nFor instance, if S= ?0?, we have T=\\lbrace 000_{(2)},001_{(2)},100_{(2)},101_{(2)}\\rbrace=\\lbrace 0,1,4,5\\rbrace.\nPrint (as a decimal integer) the greatest value in T less than or equal to N.\nIf T does not contain a value less than or equal to N, print -1 instead.\n\nInput\n\nThe input is given from Standard Input in the following format:\nS\nN\n\nOutput\n\nPrint the answer.\n\nConstraints\n\n\n- S is a string consisting of 0, 1, and ?.\n- The length of S is between 1 and 60, inclusive.\n- 1\\leq N \\leq 10^{18}\n- N is an integer.\n\nSample Input 1\n\n?0?\n2\n\nSample Output 1\n\n1\n\nAs shown in the problem statement, T=\\lbrace 0,1,4,5\\rbrace.\nAmong them, 0 and 1 are less than or equal to N, so you should print the greatest of them, 1.\n\nSample Input 2\n\n101\n4\n\nSample Output 2\n\n-1\n\nWe have T=\\lbrace 5\\rbrace, which does not contain a value less than or equal to N.\n\nSample Input 3\n\n?0?\n1000000000000000000\n\nSample Output 3\n\n5\n", "role": "user"}], "chat_messages_sha256": "sha256:ebdcc8552b2d920461274443a8dab57a49842f2d604645c56071bbcb33e64f69", "code_extraction": {"method": "raw_stdout", "status": "no_code_block"}, "completion_token_count": 384, "content_hash": "sha256:2e8bca6765bea3554a9848cf3cafe3cd3d703d3476eea2deceb17c4b49259475", "entry_point": "solve", "extracted_code": "The problem asks us to find the maximum integer value in the set $T$ that is less than or equal to a given integer $N$.\n$T$ is formed by replacing each '?' in string $S$ with either '0' or '1', and interpreting the resulting binary string as an integer.\n$S$ has length between 1 and 60. $N \\le 10^{18}$.\n\nLet $L$ be the length of $S$. The maximum possible value in $T$ is when all '?' are replaced by '1', which gives a binary number of length $L$. If $L > 60$, the value could exceed $2^{60}$, but $N \\le 10^{18} < 2^{60}$. Actually, $2^{60} \\approx 1.15 \\times 10^{18}$, so $L$ up to 60 is fine. Python handles large integers automatically.\n\nWe want $\\max \\{ v \\in T \\mid v \\le N \\}$. If no such $v$ exists, output -1.\n\nLet's denote the binary string corresponding to $N$ as $B_N$. Since $N \\le 10^{18}$, $B_N$ has at most 60 bits.\nThe length of $S$ is $L$.\nIf $L > \\text{length}(B_N)$, then any number formed by $S$ will have more bits than $N$, so it will be greater than $N$ (unless leading zeros are allowed, but the problem says \"interpreting the result as a binary integer\", which usually means standard binary representation without leading zeros, except for 0 itself. However, $S$ is given as a string of fixed", "extracted_code_sha256": "sha256:050d55e3470ccb1e09f0a11e0aef7020149a3a45e25cf2a7cf00a20d95d3a591", "finish_reason": "length", "max_tokens": 384, "model_family": "qwen3", "model_hf_id": "unsloth/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-GGUF", "model_name": "Qwen3.6-35B-A3B", "model_path": "/home/ianblenke/.cache/huggingface/hub/models--unsloth--Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-GGUF/snapshots/a483e9e6cbd595906af30beda3187c2663a1118c/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-UD-Q4_K_M.gguf", "model_quantization": "UD-Q4_K_M", "model_revision": "a483e9e6cbd595906af30beda3187c2663a1118c", "n_ctx": 4096, "order_index": 6, "private_test_sha256": "sha256:955f0b12f4be6439c69cc8abb5a49a0fa122e2f80212ef09a7ced60a1c4619f0", "pr