lass has 0 milliliters, and the mug has 200 milliliters of water.\n- Transfer water from the mug to the glass until the mug is empty. The glass has 200 milliliters, and the mug has 0 milliliters of water.\n- Fill the mug with water. The glass has 200 milliliters, and the mug has 500 milliliters of water.\n\nThus, after five operations, the glass has 200 milliliters, and the mug has 500 milliliters of water.\nHence, print 200 and 500 in this order, separated by a space.\n\nSample Input 2\n\n5 100 200\n\nSample Output 2\n\n0 0\n", "role": "user"}], "chat_messages_sha256": "sha256:9021314efe3c9f6c0beea95daccc8c1676293ae198977d2d6ff9f526e9ba52e3", "code_extraction": {"method": "fenced_code_block", "status": "ok"}, "completion_token_count": 334, "content_hash": "sha256:caa3d76d988a19066da7194afe874674b9afacdaf875871af3294cea36cf319b", "entry_point": "solve", "extracted_code": "import sys\n\ndef solve():\n    # Explicit parsing of input\n    input_data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if not input_data:\n        return\n    \n    K = int(input_data[0])\n    G = int(input_data[1])\n    M = int(input_data[2])\n\n    # Initial state\n    glass = 0\n    mug = 0\n\n    # Boundary case: K = 0 (though constraints say K >= 1)\n    if K == 0:\n        print(f\"{glass} {mug}\")\n        return\n\n    # General case simulation\n    for _ in range(K):\n        # Rule 1: If glass is full, discard all water from glass\n        if glass == G:\n            glass = 0\n        # Rule 2: Otherwise, if mug is empty, fill the mug\n        elif mug == 0:\n            mug = M\n        # Rule 3: Otherwise, transfer water from mug to glass\n        else:\n            # Amount we can potentially move is limited by what's in the mug\n            # and how much space is left in the glass\n            space_in_glass = G - glass\n            transfer_amount = min(mug, space_in_glass)\n            \n            glass += transfer_amount\n            mug -= transfer_amount\n\n    # Final output\n    print