rm the following operations: $$\\texttt{WW}\\color{red}{\\texttt{BWB}}\\texttt{WW} \\to \\texttt{WWWWWWW}$$\n\nIn the third test case you can perform the following operations: $$\\texttt{B}\\color{red}{\\texttt{WBWB}} \\to \\color{red}{\\texttt{BWWW}}\\texttt{W} \\to \\texttt{WWWWW}$$\n", "role": "user"}], "chat_messages_sha256": "sha256:5f11b9c7a14e0631b34af1f9254495bb07c43fdbebed5f86db9aa92e8ac00749", "code_extraction": {"method": "fenced_code_block", "status": "ok"}, "completion_token_count": 264, "content_hash": "sha256:1118a08eae600a68b0d8a77ef4c7f0c17308099b46039324bb647c809b01ea64", "entry_point": "solve", "extracted_code": "import sys\n\ndef solve():\n    input_data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if not input_data:\n        return\n    \n    t = int(input_data[0])\n    ptr = 1\n    results = []\n    \n    for _ in range(t):\n        n = int(input_data[ptr])\n        k = int(input_data[ptr + 1])\n        s = input_data[ptr + 2]\n        ptr += 3\n        \n        ops = 0\n        i = 0\n        while i < n:\n            if s[i] == 'B':\n                # If we encounter a black cell, we must use an operation.\n                # To be optimal (greedy), we start the k-length eraser here.\n                ops += 1\n                i += k\n            else:\n                # If it's white, just move to the next cell.\n                i += 1\n        results.append(str(ops))\n    \n    sys.stdout.write('\\n'.join(results) + '\\n')\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    solve()", "extracted_code_sha256": "sha256:719ba423d9cff97fe2abcafe763495e7ae272e141f2cfe5ab80c66ffdf4b7d10", "finish_reason": "stop", "max_tokens": 384, "model_family": "gemma4", "model_hf_id": "unsloth/gemma-4-26B-A4B-it-GGUF", "model_name": "Gemma4-26B-A4B-it", "model_path": "/home/ianblenke/.cache/huggingface/hub/models--unsloth--gemma-4-26B-A4B-it-GGUF/snapshots/3365c68df1a83799b846d05324ebfadbb8cc70b3/gemma-4-26B-A4B-it-UD-Q4_K_M.gguf", "model_quantization": "UD-Q4_K_M", "model_revision": "33