+{"cell_id": "sha256:f4991132c87c031875e73fb0edc2b69e3e491680056075f81858b3df85f09abe", "chat_messages": [{"content": "You are writing one Python solution for a programming task. Return only raw Python code or one fenced python block. Do not explain the answer.", "role": "system"}, {"content": "Seed cell: sha256:f4991132c87c031875e73fb0edc2b69e3e491680056075f81858b3df85f09abe\nStrategy: edge_case_guarded\nWrite a Python solution that handles boundary cases first, then the general case. Keep parsing explicit and return only runnable code.\n\nTitle: Anti\nA DDoS-type string is a string of length 4 consisting of uppercase and lowercase English letters satisfying both of the following conditions.\n\n- The first, second, and fourth characters are uppercase English letters, and the third character is a lowercase English letter.\n- The first and second characters are equal.\n\nFor instance, DDoS and AAaA are DDoS-type strings, while neither ddos nor IPoE is.\nYou are given a string S consisting of uppercase and lowercase English letters and ?.\nLet q be the number of occurrences of ? in S. There are 52^q strings that can be obtained by independently replacing each ? in S with an uppercase or lowercase English letter.\nAmong these strings, find the number of ones that do not contain a DDoS-type string as a subsequence, modulo 998244353.\n\nInput\n\nThe input is given from Standard Input in the following format:\nS\n\nOutput\n\nPrint the answer.\n\nConstraints\n\n\n- S consists of uppercase English letters, lowercase English letters, and ?.\n- The length of S is between 4 and 3\\times 10^5, inclusive.\n\nSample Input 1\n\nDD??S\n\nSample Output 1\n\n676\n\nWhen at least one of the ?s is replaced with a lowercase English letter, the resulting string will contain a DDoS-type string as a subsequence.\n\nSample Input 2\n\n????????????????????????????????????????\n\nSample Output 2\n\n858572093\n\nFind the count modulo 998244353.\n\nSample Input 3\n\n?D??S\n\nSample Output 3\n\n136604\n", "role": "user"}], "chat_messages_sha256": "sha256:cfc3d2566291ce16d95a2cdfd45885f64ca84ed55287f50270b661d785157be3", "code_extraction": {"method": "raw_stdout", "status": "no_code_block"}, "completion_token_count": 384, "content_hash": "sha256:d6de3cf9484f396c5a45200b5cacf63594332c9f5abfb241d38c113ac1f3b2b6", "entry_point": "solve", "extracted_code": "```python\nimport sys\n\ndef solve():\n    s = sys.stdin.readline().strip()\n    if not s:\n        return\n    \n    n = len(s)\n    MOD = 998244353\n\n    # A DDoS-type string is a subsequence of length 4:\n    # S[i], S[j], S[k], S[l] where i < j < k < l\n    # Condition: S[i], S[j], S[l] are uppercase, S[k] is lowercase, and S[i] == S[j].\n    \n    # To avoid a DDoS-type subsequence, we must not have:\n    # (Uppercase char X) at index i, (Same Uppercase char X) at index j,\n    # (Any Lowercase char) at index k, (Any Uppercase char) at index l\n    # where i < j < k < l.\n\n    # Let's rephrase: We want to avoid the pattern (X, X, lowercase, uppercase).\n    # This is equivalent to saying that for any pair of identical uppercase letters at indices i and j (i < j),\n    # there are no lowercase letters at index k > j AND no uppercase letters at index l > k.\n    # Wait, the condition is: there exists i < j < k < l such that S[i]=S[j]=X (upper), S[k]=lower, S[l]=upper.\n\n    # Let's use DP. \n    # A string contains a DDoS-type subsequence if there exist indices i < j < k < l such that:\n    # S[i] == S[j] (both uppercase), S[k] is lowercase,", "extracted_code_sha256": "sha256:602b016743750386e60fb973329ea092861ad12cbdb1835a1e39b5dc68d04f42", "finish_reason": "length", "max_tokens": 384, "model_family": "gemma4", "model_hf_id": "unsloth/gemma-4-26B-A4B-it-GGUF", "model_name": "Gemma4-26B-A4B-it", "model_path": "/home/ianblenke/.cache/huggingface/hub/models--unsloth--gemma-4-26B-A4B-it-GGUF/snapshots/3365c68df1a83799b846d05324ebfadbb8cc70b3/gemma-4-26B-A4B-it-UD-Q4_K_M.gguf", "model_quantization": "UD-Q4_