quare numbers that can be obtained by interpreting a permutation of S\". This implies we count distinct values. Sample 2 confirms this: permutations resulting in 1 and 100 are counted, but multiple permutations yielding the same number don't increase the count.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Count the frequency of each digit in $S$. Let's call this `target_counts`.", "raw_stdout_sha256": "sha256:21c6a906d4d2fb9443a8f53108194456ffc96fd1453c36150dccf85e0aa80617", "refusal": false, "repeat_penalty": 1.05, "row_hash": "sha256:7a5089ba506692cece06be8cdf6e700df79b63cd9f16f1b3240cd95ae791f330", "run_date": "20260807", "runtime": "python_stdio", "schema": "carnot.experiment_6192.live_strategy_seed_stream.v1.raw_row", "seed": 619200038, "selector_features": {"date_bucket": "2023-Q4", "difficulty": "hard", "platform": "atcoder", "prompt_size_bucket": "short", "supported_runtime": "python_stdio", "tag_bucket": "untagged"}, "split": "csl_seed", "stable_task_hash": "sha256:25cb7cfb339b83675a3b811a8794ea9ee68e787dd93c3f97a1cf59db0d7cfb11", "strategy_id": "direct_implementation", "strategy_prompt_sha256": "sha256:0936e7f99b76be2579a31a16fbd66f368cbe79e1ce12b726f67bd7f08213bf2f", "task_id": "abc324_d", "temperature": 0.0, "timeout": false, "timing": {"decode_time_s": 3.30443, "started_monotonic_s": 1212927.153702}, "top_k": 40, "top_p": 1.0, "transport_failure": false, "truncated": true}
+{"cell_id": "sha256:cccf6c740776a591e885d277ffe7fab2a0ec6e7b90f26574359f853625bca92d", "chat_messages": [{"content": "You are writing one Python solution for a programming task. Return only raw Python code or one fenced python block. Do not explain the answer.", "role": "system"}, {"content": "Seed cell: sha256:cccf6c740776a591e885d277ffe7fab2a0ec6e7b90f26574359f853625bca92d\nStrategy: direct_implementation\nImplement the requested Python solution directly. Prefer clear control flow, standard input/output handling when no starter function is provided, and return only runnable code.\n\nTitle: Chords\nThere are 2N points placed at equal intervals on a circle, numbered 1 to 2N in a clockwise direction starting from a certain point.\nThere are also N chords on the circle, with the i-th chord connecting points A_i and B_i.\nIt is guaranteed that all the values A_1,\\dots,A_N,B_1,\\dots,B_N are distinct.\nDetermine whether there is an intersection between the chords.\n\nInput\n\nThe input is given from Standard Input in the following format:\nN\nA_1 B_1\nA_2 B_2\n\\vdots\nA_N B_N\n\nOutput\n\nIf there is an intersection between the chords, print Yes; otherwise, print No.\n\nConstraints\n\n\n- 2\\leq N \\leq 2\\times 10^5\n- 1\\leq A_i,B_i \\leq 2N\n- A_1,\\dots,A_N,B_1,\\dots,B_N are all distinct\n- All input values are integers\n\nSample Input 1\n\n3\n1 3\n4 2\n5 6\n\nSample Output 1\n\nYes\n\n\nAs shown in the figure, chord 1 (the line segment connecting points 1 and 3) and chord 2 (the line segment connecting points 4 and 2) intersect, so print Yes.\n\nSample Input 2\n\n3\n6 1\n4 3\n2 5\n\nSample Output 2\n\nNo\n\n\nAs shown in the figure, there is no intersection between the chords, so print No.\n\nSample Input 3\n\n4\n2 4\n3 7\n8 6\n5 1\n\nSample Output 3\n\nYes\n", "role": "user"}], "chat_messages_sha256": "sha256:fb8545d32c8236db299a2c4c18b67ec543a0ee887d76dd553953894bbc8d6671", "code_extraction": {"method": "raw_stdout", "status": "no_code_block"}, "completion_to