total amount for the products is not less than 2000 yen, the shipping fee will be 0 yen.\nTherefore, the amount Takahashi will pay is 6600+0=6600 yen.\n\nSample Input 3\n\n2 2000 500\n1000 1\n1000 1\n\nSample Output 3\n\n2000\n\nThere may be multiple products with the same price per item.\n", "role": "user"}], "chat_messages_sha256": "sha256:9114cf8e5e64a84bc68a297e66f24ea999b2c89b88ad2744c34c8a4f4c556b05", "code_extraction": {"method": "raw_stdout", "status": "no_code_block"}, "completion_token_count": 384, "content_hash": "sha256:7e207aaa73170b2d7adcc3c65a27b8a0a01c6cb66e7e81fdddae8616659067b2", "entry_point": "solve", "extracted_code": "The problem asks us to calculate the total cost of an online shopping purchase.\nWe are given:\n- $N$: number of product types.\n- $S$: threshold for free shipping.\n- $K$: shipping fee if the total price is less than $S$.\n- For each product type $i$, we have price $P_i$ and quantity $Q_i$.\n\nThe total cost is calculated as follows:\n1. Calculate the sum of prices for all products: $\\text{Total Price} = \\sum_{i=1}^{N} P_i \\times Q_i$.\n2. If $\\text{Total Price} \\ge S$, shipping fee is 0.\n3. Otherwise, shipping fee is $K$.\n4. Total amount to pay = $\\text{Total Price} + \\text{Shipping Fee}$.\n\nLet's verify with Sample 1:\nN=2, S=2000, K=500\nProduct 1: P=1000, Q=1 -> cost = 1000\nProduct 2: P=100, Q=6 -> cost = 600\nTotal Price = 1600.\nSince 1600 < 2000, shipping fee = 500.\nTotal pay = 1600 + 500 = 2100. Matches sample output.\n\nSample 2:\nN=3, S=2000, K=500\nProduct 1: 1000*1 = 1000\nProduct 2: 100*6 = 600\nProduct 3: 5000*1 = 5000\nTotal Price = 6", "extracted_code_sha256": "sha256:8be4cede0c2dbdd6384b1583b5d8e8ac54e6cd41c0358f2fd6037ef2278cadba", "finish_reason": "length", "max_tokens": 384, "model_family": "qwen3", "model_hf_id": "unsloth/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-GGUF", "model_name": "Qwen3.6-35B-A3B", "model_path": "/home/ianblenke/.cache/huggingface/hub/models--unsloth--Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-GGUF/snapshots/a483e9e6cbd595906af3