+{"cell_id": "sha256:5aa38e2b1937e873296b25f230baa8717e9467cc45b10d96e11d73c8b7c4ad81", "chat_messages": [{"content": "You are writing one Python solution for a programming task. Return only raw Python code or one fenced python block. Do not explain the answer.", "role": "system"}, {"content": "Seed cell: sha256:5aa38e2b1937e873296b25f230baa8717e9467cc45b10d96e11d73c8b7c4ad81\nStrategy: invariant_first\nBefore writing code, identify the key invariant or recurrence and then encode it compactly. Return only the final Python code.\n\nTitle: Invisible Hand\nThere are N sellers and M buyers in an apple market.\nThe i-th seller may sell an apple for A_i yen or more (yen is the currency in Japan).\nThe i-th buyer may buy an apple for B_i yen or less.\nFind the minimum integer X that satisfies the following condition.\nCondition: The number of people who may sell an apple for X yen is greater than or equal to the number of people who may buy an apple for X yen.\n\nInput\n\nThe input is given from Standard Input in the following format:\nN M\r\nA_1 \\ldots A_N\r\nB_1 \\ldots B_M\n\nOutput\n\nPrint the answer.\n\nConstraints\n\n\n- 1 \\leq N,M \\leq 2\\times 10^5\n- 1\\leq A_i,B_i \\leq 10^9\n- All input values are integers.\n\nSample Input 1\n\n3 4\r\n110 90 120\r\n100 80 120 10000\n\nSample Output 1\n\n110\r\n\nTwo sellers, the 1-st and 2-nd, may sell an apple for 110 yen; two buyers, the 3-rd and 4-th, may buy an apple for 110 yen.  Thus, 110 satisfies the condition.\nSince an integer less than 110 does not satisfy the condition, this is the answer.\n\nSample Input 2\n\n5 2\r\n100000 100000 100000 100000 100000\r\n100 200\n\nSample Output 2\n\n201\n\nSample Input 3\n\n3 2\r\n100 100 100\r\n80 120\n\nSample Output 3\n\n100\n", "role": "user"}], "chat_messages_sha256": "sha256:a61bf8f6a9bc7fdac360d5ddc6090dad80a7995667e82c00c73ba88aa11dae23", "code_extraction": {"method": "raw_stdout", "status": "no_code_block"}, "completion_token_count": 384, "content_hash": "sha256:520d8596ba6e686d4127ca1ee00ef3a609091e469f0dd93177ae519e329f87c2", "entry_point": "solve", "extracted_code": "```python\nimport sys\nimport bisect\n\ndef solve():\n    input_data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if not input_data:\n        return\n    \n    N = int(input_data[0])\n    M = int(input_data[1])\n    \n    A = sorted([int(x) for x in input_data[2:2+N]])\n    B = sorted([int(x) for x in input_data[2+N:2+N+M]])\n    \n    # Condition: count(A_i <= X) >= count(B_j >= X)\n    # Let f(X) = count(A_i <= X) - count(B_j >= X)\n    # We want minimum X such that f(X) >= 0.\n    # Note: count(B_j >= X) = M - count(B_j < X)\n    # So condition is: count(A_i <= X) + count(B_j < X) >= M\n    \n    low = 1\n    high = 2 * 10**9 # Sufficiently large upper bound\n    ans = high\n    \n    while low <= high:\n        mid = (low + high) // 2\n        \n        # count(A_i <= mid)\n        count_A = bisect.bisect_right(A, mid)\n        # count(B_j < mid)\n        count_B_less = bisect.bisect_left(B, mid)\n        \n        if count_A + count_B_less >= M:\n            ans = mid\n            high = mid - 1\n        else:\n            low", "extracted_code_sha256": "sha256:8bf8a7af4a1c4bd429738a54ec2784af737a660236763a762b9100b1bc04b69f", "finish_reason": "length", "max_tokens": 384, "model_family": "gemma4", "model_hf_id": "unsloth/gemma-4-26B-A4B-it-GGUF", "model_name": "Gemma4-26B-A4B-it", "model_path": "/home/ianblenke/.cache/huggingface/hub/models--unsloth--gemma-4-26B-A4B-it-GGUF/snapshots/3365c68df1a83799b846d05324ebfadbb8cc70b3/gemma-4-26B-A4B-it-UD-Q4_K_M.gguf", "model_quantization": "UD-Q4_K_M", "model_revision": "3365c68df1a83799b846d05324ebfadbb8cc70b3", "n_ctx": 4096, "order_index": 85, "private_test_sha256": "sha256:b4a5ed249252f094152319dfac1594820649aa20be1592e8035dfc194d0b8250", "prompt_sha256": "sha256:43673cb36ce47eb61bdc55c7b8a9ba7adb0d9bbfe347720446aed2d7e3ef4a45", "prompt_token_count": 579, "public_test_sha256": "sha256:dbba271a592a6cf2b63a8eb30a0b9d1a55f42776c87