50d865b6a550852620404e58ca13cd7be63b1c7", "entry_point": "solve", "extracted_code": "The problem asks us to find the maximum integer value in a set $T$ that is less than or equal to $N$.\nThe set $T$ is formed by replacing each '?' in a binary string $S$ with either '0' or '1'.\n$S$ has length up to 60. $N$ is up to $10^{18}$.\n\nLet $L$ be the length of $S$. The values in $T$ are integers between $0$ and $2^L - 1$.\nSince $L \\le 60$, the values can be quite large, but $N$ is also up to $10^{18} \\approx 2^{60}$. So we need to handle 64-bit integers. Python handles arbitrarily large integers automatically, so overflow is not an issue.\n\nWe want to maximize $x \\in T$ such that $x \\le N$.\nLet's denote the binary representation of $N$ as a string $B_N$. Note that $S$ might have length different from the number of bits in $N$. However, since we are comparing values, we can think of them as numbers.\n\nLet's process the string $S$ from left to right (most significant bit to least significant bit).\nWe want to construct a binary string $S'$ corresponding to some value in $T$ such that the integer value of $S'$ is $\\le N$ and maximized.\n\nLet $L$ be the length of $S$.\nIf $L > 60$, $2^L - 1$ can exceed $N$. But constraints say $L \\le 60$.\nActually, if $L >$ number of bits in $N$, it's possible that all values in $T$ are greater than $N", "extracted_code_sha256": "sha256:5ee6c3fd19fa16c4fbbee7e87332167f597e207ddc6f5a9302f7070786db70c8", "finish_reason": "length", "max_tokens": 384, "model_family": "qwen3", "model_hf_id": "unsloth/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-GGUF", "model_name": "Qwen3.6-35B-A3B", "model_path": "/home/ianblenke/.cache/huggingface/hub/models--unsloth--Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-GGUF/snapshots/a483e9e6cbd595906af30beda3187c2663a1118c/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-UD-Q4_K_M.gguf", "model_quantization": "UD-Q4_K_M", "model_revision": "a483e9e6cbd595906af30beda3187c2663a1118c", "n_ctx": 4096, "order_index": 94, "private_test_sha256": "sha256:955f0b12f4be6439c69cc8abb5a49a0fa122e2f80212ef09a