+{"cell_id": "sha256:a222747d2421f7f1df039b104adfe78438bf1aaaf3bbec1a51fecc3ac66c9b23", "chat_messages": [{"content": "You are writing one Python solution for a programming task. Return only raw Python code or one fenced python block. Do not explain the answer.", "role": "system"}, {"content": "Seed cell: sha256:a222747d2421f7f1df039b104adfe78438bf1aaaf3bbec1a51fecc3ac66c9b23\nStrategy: invariant_first\nBefore writing code, identify the key invariant or recurrence and then encode it compactly. Return only the final Python code.\n\nTitle: Standings\nN people numbered 1 through N tossed a coin several times.  We know that person i's tosses resulted in A_i heads and B_i tails.\nPerson i's success rate of the tosses is defined by \\displaystyle\\frac{A_i}{A_i+B_i}.  Sort people 1,\\ldots,N in descending order of their success rates, with ties broken in ascending order of their assigned numbers.\n\nInput\n\nThe input is given from Standard Input in the following format:\nN\r\nA_1 B_1\r\n\\vdots\r\nA_N B_N\n\nOutput\n\nPrint the numbers of people 1,\\ldots,N in descending order of their success rates, with ties broken in ascending order of their assigned numbers.\n\nConstraints\n\n\n- 2\\leq N \\leq 2\\times 10^5\n- 0\\leq A_i, B_i\\leq 10^9\n- A_i+B_i \\geq 1\n- All input values are integers.\n\nSample Input 1\n\n3\r\n1 3\r\n3 1\r\n2 2\n\nSample Output 1\n\n2 3 1\r\n\nPerson 1's success rate is 0.25, person 2's is 0.75, and person 3's is 0.5.\nSort them in descending order of their success rates to obtain the order in Sample Output.\n\nSample Input 2\n\n2\r\n1 3\r\n2 6\n\nSample Output 2\n\n1 2\r\n\nNote that person 1 and 2 should be printed in ascending order of their numbers, as they have the same success rates.\n\nSample Input 3\n\n4\r\n999999999 1000000000\r\n333333333 999999999\r\n1000000000 999999997\r\n999999998 1000000000\n\nSample Output 3\n\n3 1 4 2\n", "role": "user"}], "chat_messages_sha256": "sha256:13f229e6f4c7550f42f378fca2743d36cff672770b7760a59be804045361f11a", "code_extraction": {"method": "raw_stdout", "status": "no_code_block"}, "completion_token_count": 384, "content_hash": "sha256:5fc92952f159904badfbae8255cd6cc6e6ce831efb58071d3ef26b5d68e5d4b2", "entry_point": "solve", "extracted_code": "```python\nimport sys\nfrom functools import cmp_to_key\n\ndef solve():\n    input_data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if not input_data:\n        return\n    \n    N = int(input_data[0])\n    people = []\n    idx = 1\n    for i in range(1, N + 1):\n        a = int(input_data[idx])\n        b = int(input_data[idx+1])\n        # Success rate is a / (a + b)\n        # To compare a1/(a1+b1) and a2/(a2+b2) without floats:\n        # a1 * (a2 + b2) vs a2 * (a1 + b1)\n        people.append((a, b, i))\n        idx += 2\n\n    def compare(p1, p2):\n        a1, b1, id1 = p1\n        a2, b2, id2 = p2\n        \n        # Compare a1/(a1+b1) and a2/(a2+b2)\n        # val1 = a1 * (a2 + b2)\n        # val2 = a2 * (a1 + b1)\n        v1 = a1 * (a2 + b2)\n        v2 = a2 * (a1 + b1)\n        \n        if v1 > v2:\n            return -1\n        elif v1 < v2:\n            return 1\n        else:\n            # Tie-break: ascending order of IDs\n            if id1 < id2:\n                return -1\n            else:\n                return 1", "extracted_code_sha256": "sha256:96ad98cea976d7cbb1f1fedd507ef7809d9dce01a9a2faef08106c1ed72b6237", "finish_reason": "length", "max_tokens": 384, "model_family": "gemma4", "model_hf_id": "unsloth/gemma-4-26B-A4B-it-GGUF", "model_name": "Gemma4-26B-A4B-it", "model_path": "/home/ianblenke/.cache/huggingface/hub/models--unsloth--gemma-4-26B-A4B-it-GGUF/snapshots/3365c68df1a83799b846d05324ebfadbb8cc70b3/gemma-4-26B-A4B-it-UD-Q4_K_M.gguf", "model_quantization": "UD-Q4_K_M", "model_revision": "3365c68df1a83799b846d05324ebfadbb8cc70b3", "n_ctx": 4096, "order_index": 96, "private_test_sha256": "sha256:89afb067efa5e89cbcee7ee4c5ae94086d12788d7135cdc4e8ffc261f0992b81", "prompt_sha256": "sha256:2ec7f7f3c86025d72808